<title>SINGAPORE: Glencore wins Bombay low aromatic naphtha at -$27.</title>
<headline>Glencore wins Bombay low aromatic naphtha at -$27.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has awarded Swiss trader Glencore its sell tender for low aromatic naphtha (LAN) from Bombay on the west coast at $27 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 30,000-tonne cargo lifting May 27-29 was awarded on a free-on-board (fob) basis in a tender which closed May 15 and was valid for a day.  </p>
<p>IOC's last Bombay LAN cargo, lifting May 17-19, was awarded to German trader Stinnes at $53 per tonne below U.S. Gulf Coast 87-octane gasoline spot waterbourne quotes, fob, or equivalent to a $25-$30 per tonne discount to Japanese spot quotes.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
